      "content": "here's the data from one of the affected nodes. \n\ntraceroute:\n1. 192.168.1.1 (gateway) - 1ms\n2. 10.25.44.1 - 12ms\n3. 172.16.0.5 - 45ms\n4. 172.16.0.8 - 240ms *\n5. 172.16.0.9 - 215ms *\n6. 172.16.0.12 - 18ms (back to normal)\n\nping stats (64 byte packets):\n64 bytes from 172.16.0.8: icmp_seq=1 ttl=56 time=210.4 ms\n64 bytes from 172.16.0.8: icmp_seq=2 ttl=56 time=245.1 ms\n64 bytes from 172.16.0.8: icmp_seq=3 ttl=56 time=12.3 ms\n64 bytes from 172.16.0.8: icmp_seq=4 ttl=56 * (request timeout)\n64 bytes from 172.16.0.8: icmp_seq=5 ttl=56 time=233.7 ms\n\nhop 4 and 5 are spiking hard then it drops back down at hop 6. what's your take? is it a bad port/cable or something with the routing table?",
