      "content": "Yes, that kind of intermittent behavior over time is highly characteristic of physical layer issues like electromagnetic interference, loose connectors causing overheating, or illumination on damaged fiber. While \"gremlins\" usually refers to carrier bugs, real-world hardware degradation like corroded pins or cable stress can indeed create random packet loss and high jitter. Check for loose cables, overheating equipment, or nearby electrical sources as these are likely culprits.",
